Bailey will find the volume of a rectangular prism by filling it with cubes that measure 1 cubic inch. She has not yet finished filling the prism. Her progress is shown in the figure below.

\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.6]
% Draw the rectangular prism outline
\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (3,0) -- (3,4) -- (0,4) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] (0,4) -- (1.5,5.5) -- (4.5,5.5) -- (3,4);
\draw[thick] (3,0) -- (4.5,1.5) -- (4.5,5.5);
% Draw the cubes at the bottom layer
\foreach \x in {0,1,2} {
  \foreach \y in {0,1,2,3} {
    \draw (\x,\y) rectangle (\x+1,\y+1);
  }
}
% Labels
\node[left] at (0,2) {5 in.};
\node[below] at (1.5,0) {3 in.};
\node[right] at (4.5,3) {4 in.};
\end{tikzpicture}

What is the total volume, in cubic inches, of the prism?
